     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and serious GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nAlso, medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one. I can't confirm that this order has been through that process.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **If the dose was a typo**, tell me the intended dose. For example, 850 mg three times daily with meals is 2,550 mg/day, and 500 mg three times daily is 1,500 mg/day. I can enter it once a prescriber confirms it.\n- **If the dose is intended**, the treating prescriber should enter or confirm it directly, with their clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note documenting that.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
