     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems.\n\n- **The dose is unsafe.** 5,100 mg/day is about double the maximum labeled dose. It has no clinical justification I can see, and it puts the patient at real risk of lactic acidosis.\n- **There's no prescriber authorization.** You've said you're not a clinician, so your confirmation can't serve as clinical verification of the dose.\n\n**What to do next:**\n1. Have the patient's treating prescriber review the intended dose and enter it themselves. If they really mean a dose this high, they can document the rationale and go through pharmacy verification.\n2. If the order was meant to be a standard dose, the prescriber can tell me, and I'll enter it right away. For example, 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals is 2,550 mg/day.\n\nI can also enter a safe order once a clinician gives me the dose."
      }
     ],
